rly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}\\le \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le {x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1}\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & \\le \\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}-\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\le U(f,P).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{1}{2}({6}^{2}-{0}^{2})(2-1)=18 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{1}{2}({2}^{2}-{1}^{2})(6-0)=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le 18-9\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le 9\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=9.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
